# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

Contributions are welcome and appreciated.

## Ways to help

- Report a bug
- Propose a new feature
- Improve the documentation
- Submit a fix

## Getting set up

This project uses [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv). Install it first, then:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ github_username }}/{{ github_repo }}.git
cd {{ github_repo }}
uv sync --all-groups
uv run pre-commit install
```

## Before opening a pull request

```bash
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check --fix .
uv run pytest
uv run ty check
```

The first three must pass. `ty check` is advisory while ty is pre-1.0.

## Branching

- `main` is stable and always releasable.
- Work on topic branches named `feature/...` or `fix/...`.
- Open the pull request against `main`.

## Reporting bugs

Open an issue using the bug report template. A good report includes:

- A short summary and the context.
- Steps to reproduce, with sample code if possible.
- What you expected to happen, and what happened instead.
- Your Python version and operating system.

